%S A399827 0,0,0,1,13,378,17068,1382794,205784194,58112091184,31713315324824,
%T A399827 33827342775504936,71066544335217392696,295645501996821684383648,
%U A399827 2444503528640608508920456400,40269655262779228730821692093968
%N A399827 Number of labeled mating graphs whose family of open neighborhoods is connected.
%C A399827 A mating graph is a graph in which no two distinct vertices have the same open neighborhood.
%C A399827 The family of open neighborhoods is connected if its intersection graph is connected, where two members are adjacent when they have nonempty intersection.
%C A399827 a(n) is the number of connected nonbipartite labeled mating graphs on n vertices.
%H A399827 I. M. Gessel and J. Li, <a href="https://people.brandeis.edu/~gessel/homepage/papers/pd.pdf">Enumeration of Point-Determining Graphs</a>, Journal of Combinatorial Theory, Series A 118 (2011), 591-612.
%H A399827 Ira M. Gessel and Ji Li, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcta.2010.03.009">Enumeration of point-determining graphs</a>, J. Combinatorial Theory Ser. A 118 (2011), 591-612.
%F A399827 a(n) = A092430(n) - A232700(n), since the intersection graph of the open-neighborhood family {N_G(v) : v in V(G)} is connected iff G is connected and nonbipartite.
%e A399827 a(3) = 1, corresponding to K_3, the only connected nonbipartite mating graph on 3 labeled vertices.
%Y A399827 Cf. A006024 (labeled mating graphs), A092430 (labeled connected mating graphs), A232700 (labeled connected bipartite point-determining graphs), A399826 (labeled graphs whose family of open neighborhoods is connected).
%K A399827 nonn,new
%O A399827 0,5
